 ## Models and secrets
 
 The configuration service supports account lists, per-account routes, and a default account. Routes may look like `account-...`. Select the route/model returned by the interface; do not assume all accounts for a provider share one route. Catalogs and contracts determine capabilities, and saving validates the selected model. New defaults do not rewrite existing sessions.
 
+For a custom model outside the built-in account catalog, explicit routes in the user `profile.yaml` remain available alongside saved accounts. Saved account routes come first so their default selection is preserved. Use a distinct route name; duplicate names are rejected rather than replacing an account's endpoint or credential reference. Keep credentials in the secret adapter and place only `credentialRef` in the route.
+
 Credentials use `secret://namespace/name` references. File, environment, and vault adapters are different deployment options. Do not copy fake demo tokens into real services or expose real values in browser `publicConfig`, tool output, or environment dumps.
 
+After history compaction replaces the conversation surface, context-window checks re-estimate the retained surface until a new inference provides a fresh measurement. Summary requests retain their actual billed usage, including split summaries, but that usage is not the size of the player's current context. Measurements of the replaced surface are no longer used.
+
